title: "Aggieland Lighting and Design | Lighting Showroom in College Station, TX"
description: "Lighting showroom in College Station, TX. 75+ designer lines, ceiling fans, and a free room-by-room lighting consultation for new builds and remodels in Bryan–College Station. Walk-ins welcome."
faqs:
  - q: "Where is Aggieland Lighting and Design?"
    a: "Our showroom is at 12850 Old Wellborn Rd, Suite 400, in College Station, TX 77845 — easy to reach from anywhere in Bryan–College Station."
  - q: "Do I need an appointment?"
    a: "No. Walk-ins are welcome Monday through Friday, 9:00 to 5:00. If you'd like an hour with someone who'll go room by room through your house, book a free lighting consultation so someone is definitely free when you arrive."
  - q: "My builder hasn't sent me to you. Can I still come in?"
    a: "Yes. Whoever's building your house, you're welcome here. Dozens of builders around Bryan–College Station already work with us, and we'll work alongside yours — we'll hand them a clean fixture list with quantities, finishes and lead times."
  - q: "What brands do you carry?"
    a: "More than seventy-five designer lines, including Visual Comfort, Hubbardton Forge, Arteriors, Schonbek, Corbett, Hinkley, Hudson Valley, Mitzi, Uttermost and Electric Mirror — brands you'd otherwise drive to Houston to see."
  - q: "Do you sell ceiling fans and outdoor lighting?"
    a: "Yes. Chandeliers, pendants, vanity lights, sconces, ceiling fans, exterior lights and lamps. About a hundred fixtures and fans are on the floor at any time, and we can get thousands more."
  - q: "Can I buy online?"
    a: "Yes — our full catalog is online at shop.aggielandlighting.com. Anything you find there, you can also come see or order in the showroom, and we'll tell you honestly how it will look in your home."
  - q: "What happens if something arrives damaged or fails later?"
    a: "You call us, and we deal with the manufacturer. You never have to file a claim with a company you've never spoken to."
